      "summary": "American Electric Power (AEP) has remained in focus after its Indiana and Michigan utility proposed a significant customer rate reduction plan, aiming to lower bills despite surging demand driven by industrial and computing needs. While utilities generally lagged in a rebounding market due to rising long-dated Treasury yields, AEP's strategy involves passing on benefits of load growth to customers. The company, which owns the largest electricity transmission network in the U.S., is also repositioning legacy generation sites into energy hubs and expects substantial new load additions from computing campuses, industrial reshoring, and electrification by the end of the decade.",
